# 11. User Preferences APIs

The User Preferences APIs allow authenticated users to personalize the behavior and appearance of KnowledgeOS.

These APIs operate on the `user_preferences` table and provide a centralized mechanism for configuring AI behavior, interface settings, notification preferences, and privacy options.

Each user owns exactly one preferences record.

---

## Get User Preferences

```http
GET /api/v1/preferences
```

Purpose

Returns the authenticated user's current application preferences.

Example Response

```json
{
    "theme": "light",
    "streaming_enabled": true,
    "planner_enabled": true,
    "reviewer_enabled": true,
    "show_citations": true,
    "default_homepage": "home"
}
```

---

## Update Preferences

```http
PATCH /api/v1/preferences
```

Allows updating one or more preferences.

Supported Fields

- Theme
- Streaming
- Planner
- Reviewer
- Citation Visibility
- Default Homepage
- Sidebar State
- Notification Settings

Example Request

```json
{
    "theme": "dark",
    "streaming_enabled": false
}
```

Only the supplied fields are updated.

---

## Reset Preferences

```http
POST /api/v1/preferences/reset
```

Restores all preferences to their default values.

Useful when users want to revert accidental changes.

