# 12. Error Handling

KnowledgeOS follows a consistent error handling strategy across every API endpoint.

Every failed request returns a standardized JSON structure.

---

## Error Response Format

```json
{
    "success": false,
    "error": {
        "code": "DOCUMENT_NOT_FOUND",
        "message": "The requested document does not exist."
    }
}
```

---

## Validation Errors

```http
422 Unprocessable Entity
```

Returned when request validation fails.

Examples

- Missing required field
- Invalid UUID
- Unsupported file type
- Invalid enum value

---

## Authentication Errors

```http
401 Unauthorized
```

Returned when

- JWT expired
- Missing token
- Invalid token

---

## Authorization Errors

```http
403 Forbidden
```

Returned when users attempt to access resources belonging to another user.

---

## Resource Errors

```http
404 Not Found
```

Examples

- Document
- Folder
- Chat
- Insight

---

## Conflict Errors

```http
409 Conflict
```

Examples

- Duplicate folder
- Duplicate document (future)
- Existing resource conflict

---

## Rate Limiting

```http
429 Too Many Requests
```

Future protection against abuse.

---

## Internal Errors

```http
500 Internal Server Error
```

Unexpected server failures are logged while exposing only safe error messages to clients.

---

# 13. Response Formats

All successful responses follow a standardized structure.

---

## Success Response

```json
{
    "success": true,
    "data": {}
}
```

---

## Paginated Response

```json
{
    "success": true,
    "data": [],
    "pagination": {
        "page": 1,
        "page_size": 20,
        "total_items": 240,
        "total_pages": 12
    }
}
```

---

## Streaming Response

AI chat responses use Server-Sent Events (SSE).

```text
Token

↓

Token

↓

Token

↓

Completed
```

---

## Background Processing Response

Long-running operations return immediately.

```http
202 Accepted
```

Example

```json
{
    "status": "processing",
    "job_id": "..."
}
```

